  "final_message": "The app is complete and verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask API with SQLite storage under `./data`, password hashing (scrypt + per-user salt), bearer-token auth stored in a `tokens` table, and all endpoints (auth, notes CRUD with tag/author/q filters and paging, tags aggregate). `updated_at` bumps on every PATCH; only authors can edit/delete; tags are stored as JSON and matched case-insensitively via `json_each`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind, with:\n- Register/sign-in forms and signed-in username + sign-out in the header\n- Note list (pinned badges, search, author filter, paging, tag cloud)\n- Note page rendering plain text with preserved line breaks (`whitespace-pre-wrap`)\n- Create/edit form with comma-separated tag input, API validation messages, and delete confirmation\n\n**Verification**: ran the full API through Flask test client and a live gunicorn server (register/login/CRUD/authorization/403s/404s/filters/pagination/health/SPA routing), and `npm ci && npm run build` produces `frontend/dist` cleanly.\n\nNote: the sandbox has no Docker daemon, so I couldn't run the `Dockerfile` end-to-end, but `requirements.txt`/lock and `package-lock.json` are all in place and the entry point matches `gunicorn app:app`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
